(Using Python libraries from Zoomy.)
use python's math
use python's statistics
use python's random as dice
use python's datetime
use python's json

Create an array named scores
set scores to [72, 88, 95, 61, 79]
print "average: ", call statistics's mean with scores
print "median:  ", call statistics's median with scores
print "spread:  ", call statistics's pstdev with scores
print "hypotenuse of 3,4: ", call math's hypot with 3 and 4
print "pi to 5 places:    ", rounded math's pi to 5 places

call dice's seed with 42
print "a dice roll: ", call dice's randint with 1 and 6

Let a value be called today
set today to call datetime's date's today
print "this year is at least 2025: ", today's year is at least 2025

print call json's dumps with table with "name" as "Zoe" and "scores" as scores
